+## The `optimized` branch
+
+This branch is a benchmark variant: the port with ideas from the
+[etch](https://github.com/benwmaddox/etch) experiment applied where they fit idiomatic Rust,
+compared with the published port in etch's mixed benchmark (117 people, 60 rooms, browsers
+using Turbo, people posting). Its own differences:
+
+- **Caches versioned by what each write changes.** The response and fragment caches were keyed
+  by `PRAGMA data_version`, so any commit dropped every cached page and fragment. Now the writer
+  connection's update hook records the rows each write touches, and after commit they become
+  version bumps (`crates/db/src/changes.rs`): a message or boost moves its room's version; a
+  room's touch and the search index the activity version; a membership's read state its user's
+  version; a session made or refreshed nothing; anything else the global version, which every
+  key includes. Room pages key on global + room, the sidebar and search on global + user +
+  activity. Writes from outside this process no longer invalidate the caches.
+  `CAMPFIRE_LOG_GLOBAL_WRITES=1` logs the rows that moved the global version.
+- **Unread as counts.** `rooms.posts_count` and `memberships.seen_posts` (added at boot, with
+  the unread rooms carried over): a post writes the room and its poster, not every member's
+  row. Members connected when a post arrives see it unread too (Rails' 60-second rule is gone).
+- **Shared gzip pieces.** A page's first message is compressed on its own (it followed each
+  viewer's own layout text, so it was a different piece for every viewer), and the layout's
+  import map and stylesheet links are shared fragments.
+- `CAMPFIRE_SPLICE_{FRAGMENTS,TEXT_PIECES,TEXTS}_MB` set the gzip piece stores' budgets.
+
+etch's `bench/mix/rustopt-verify.sh` checks the branch against itself with its caches off.
+
 ## Known differences
 
 The app keeps the Rails database, storage and current cookie formats compatible. Deliberate
